 for use by module-assistant.
 .
 The NVIDIA binary driver provides optimized hardware acceleration of
 OpenGL/GLX/EGL/GLES applications via a direct-rendering X Server
 for graphics cards using NVIDIA chip sets.
 .
 PLEASE read /usr/share/doc/nvidia-open-kernel-source/README.Debian.gz
 for building information. If you want the kernel module to be automatically
 installed via DKMS, install nvidia-open-kernel-dkms instead.
 .
 The NVIDIA open driver for graphics cards supports Turing and newer chip sets.
 .
 Building the kernel modules has been tested up to Linux 6.18.

Package: nvidia-open-kernel-support
Description-md5: 6790a47ffe7f29fb1a0a127656863cc9
Description-en: NVIDIA open kernel module support files
 The NVIDIA binary driver provides optimized hardware acceleration of
